{
  "description": "Camera realness (docs/REALNESS.md) for points in the raw splat frame (marble_raw_opencv: x right, y down, z forward). Each case names its cameras (camera.json fields; pitch tilts up first, then yaw turns right), gives the photo spot's height above the floor in raw units, and uses `settings` unless it has its own. Several cameras: the highest realness counts. Expected values come from a separate calculation with explicit rotation matrices; the simple cases (straight ahead, frame edges, halfway through a fade) can be checked by hand. The TypeScript reference checks this file in Node and the shader checks it in a browser; a port to another engine must pass it too.",
  "settings": {
    "margin": 0.1,
    "near_ok": 2,
    "far_limit": 6
  },
